title: The General Strike in Central Germany
subtitle: Halle, Merseburg and the Leuna works stop.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 3 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
// the party grows month by month in 1919; between the great clashes the state of siege eases
Q.repression -= 6; Q.militancy -= 2;
if (!Q.ultraleft_gone && Q.heidelberg_outcome == 0) { Q.ultraleft_satisfaction = Math.max(Q.ultraleft_satisfaction, 30); }
var g = Math.max(1.05, Math.min(1.35, 1.24 + Q.worker_support / 200 - Q.repression / 400));
for (var d of Q.districts) { Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= g; }
// the provisional Reichswehr law of 6 March 1919
Q.army_name = 'Reichswehr';
Q.army_strength = 380;
Q.freikorps_strength += 50;
RG.districtSync();
RG.startStrike('halle', true);
RG.district('halle', {militancy: 10, repression: 8});
RG.news('Central Germany on general strike: Maercker marches into Halle', 3);
!}

= The General Strike in Central Germany

Since 24 February the miners and chemical workers of Halle and Merseburg have been on strike, and the railways and power stations with them. They want the councils written into the constitution and the mines socialised. The Independents of Halle, Wilhelm Koenen above all, lead the strike committee.

On 1 March General Maercker's volunteers marched into Halle and declared a state of siege. In Weimar the Assembly has turned what is left of the old army into a provisional **Reichswehr**, under Noske.

- @committee: Join the Independents on the strike committee.
- @fund: Send the strikers our money.
- @rising: Turn the strike into a rising.

@committee
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Koenen leads, and Halle's Independents will learn to trust us.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids sharing a committee with social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.halle_line = 2;
Q.uspd_relation += 10;
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.endStrike('halle', 'won');
!}

On 8 March the strike ends with a promise from Weimar of works councils "anchored in the constitution". It is less than the strikers wanted.

@fund
subtitle: Costs 2 funds. The strike lasts, and Halle becomes a Communist district.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The Zentrale does not have the money.
on-arrival: {!
Q.halle_line = 4;
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.district('halle', {members: 0.2, loyalty: 10});
RG.endStrike('halle', 'won');
!}

The money goes into the soup kitchens of Merseburg. Our speakers stay with the strikers to the end.

@rising
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Maercker has machine guns on the Market Square.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.halle_line = 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.district('halle', {guards: 1.5, repression: 10, militancy: 8});
RG.endStrike('halle', 'crushed');
!}

There is shooting in the streets of Halle for three days. The Leuna workers do not forget who stood with them.
